+# Hooking Manager Design Contract
+
+## 1. Atmosphere / signature
+
+Dense dark-native operator console. Information is arranged as compact rows with clear column ownership, restrained borders, and one coral accent inherited from the existing manager. The Krea2 LoRA screen should feel like a native maintenance surface, not a promotional dashboard.
+
+## 2. Color
+
+- `--bg: #1a1a2e`: application background.
+- `--surface: #16213e`: primary panel background.
+- `--surface2: #0f3460`: raised controls and secondary panels.
+- `--accent: #e94560`: selected navigation, primary actions, and focus emphasis.
+- `--accent2: #533483`: hover emphasis inherited from the application.
+- `--text: #eeeeee`: primary text.
+- `--text2: #aaaaaa`: secondary text.
+- `--border: #333333`: standard separator.
+- `--success: #4caf50`: connected and valid states.
+- `--warn: #ff9800`: unmapped and stale states.
+- `--error: #f44336`: failed load and invalid input states.
+- `--krea-row: #111c36`: compact LoRA row background.
+- `--krea-input: #0d1830`: editable field background.
+- `--krea-focus: rgba(233, 69, 96, 0.22)`: focus halo.
+- `--krea-content-width: 1200px`: maximum mapping surface width.
+- `--krea-control-height: 38px`: shared input and action height.
+
+Primary text on the application surfaces and white text on the coral accent meet the existing product contrast convention. Secondary text is used only for supporting copy and metadata.
+
+## 3. Typography
+
+- UI stack: `Segoe UI`, `Malgun Gothic`, sans-serif, retained for application consistency.
+- Screen title: `1.15rem`, weight `600`, line height `1.3`.
+- Body: `0.88rem`, weight `400`, line height `1.5`.
+- Label: `0.76rem`, weight `600`, line height `1.35`.
+- Metadata and helper text: `0.72rem`, weight `400`, line height `1.4`.
+- Filename: `Consolas`, `D2Coding`, monospace at `0.78rem`, weight `400`, line height `1.4`.
+
+## 4. Spacing
+
+Base unit is `4px`.
+
+- `--space-1: 4px`
+- `--space-2: 8px`
+- `--space-3: 12px`
+- `--space-4: 16px`
+- `--space-5: 20px`
+- `--space-6: 24px`
+- `--space-8: 32px`
+
+The Krea2 table uses `8px` row gaps, `12px` internal padding, and `16px` section gaps.
+
+## 5. Components
+
+### Krea2 toolbar
+
+Uses `--surface`, a `1px` `--border` boundary, `12px` padding, and `8px` gaps. Primary refresh uses `--accent`; secondary controls use `--surface2`. All buttons use a `6px` radius.
+
+### Krea2 resolution control
+
+Sits between the toolbar and the LoRA catalog metadata so generation settings are resolved before identity mappings. It uses `--surface`, a `1px` `--border` boundary, `12px` padding, and a two-column grid with `12px` gaps. Width and height use the shared editable input component and `--krea-control-height`. Supporting constraints use the metadata typography token. Below `700px`, fields stack into one column.
+
+### Preset LoRA routing
+
+Sits below resolution and above catalog metadata because it decides how the catalog is consumed. Each preset is one compact bordered row with a numeric preset field, an exclusive mode select, and a remove action. Modes are character matching, selected LoRAs always applied, and disabled. The always-applied mode expands an inline selection region using `--krea-row`; each selected LoRA keeps an independent strength input. The panel uses the existing surface, border, spacing, radius, and control-height tokens. Below `700px`, the route header and LoRA selection rows stack into one column without horizontal scrolling.
+
+### LoRA mapping row
+
+Desktop layout is a four-column grid: status and filename, immutable source strength, editable character name, editable applied strength. Columns are `minmax(260px, 1.6fr) 120px minmax(220px, 1fr) 180px`. Background is `--krea-row`, border is `--border`, padding is `12px`, and radius is `8px`. At `700px` and below it becomes a single column without horizontal scrolling.
+
+### Editable input
+
+Background `--krea-input`, text `--text`, border `--border`, padding `8px`, radius `6px`. Focus uses `--accent` border and `--krea-focus` halo. Invalid values use `--error`. Disabled and read-only values use `--text2`.
+
+### Status badge
+
+Plain bordered label, not a decorative pill. Mapped uses `--success`; unmapped uses `--warn`; missing uses `--error`.
+
+### Empty, loading, and error panels
+
+Use the standard row boundary and `16px` padding. Loading text uses `--text2`; empty uses `--warn`; errors use `--error` and retain the retry button.
+
+## 6. Motion
+
+Controls use the existing `0.2s` transition convention. New motion is limited to color, opacity, and transform. Reduced-motion disables transform and transition effects. No layout animation is introduced.
+
+## 7. Depth
+
+Borders and tonal stacking only. The Krea2 screen adds no drop shadows. `--bg`, `--surface`, `--krea-row`, and `--krea-input` provide the complete elevation ladder.
+
+## Do / Don't
+
+- Do keep filenames read-only and visually distinct from editable mapping fields.
+- Do make unmapped behavior explicit: no character LoRA is applied.
+- Do show the workflow source used to populate the list.
+- Do make preset routing exclusive so character identity and always-on style chains cannot activate together accidentally.
+- Do keep missing preset routes fail-closed and label that behavior in helper copy.
+- Don't use gradients, glow, glass effects, decorative status dots, or oversized cards.
+- Don't add a second accent color or a new icon family.
