+# Krea2 character LoRA UI tokens
+
+The Krea2 mapping screen extends the existing Hooking Manager visual language.
+It does not introduce a separate theme or decorative component system.
+
+## Color
+
+- Page: `--bg: #1a1a2e`
+- Primary surface: `--surface: #16213e`
+- Secondary surface: `--surface2: #0f3460`
+- Mapping row: `--krea-row: #111c36`
+- Input surface: `--krea-input: #0d1830`
+- Primary accent: `--accent: #e94560`
+- Success: `--success: #4caf50`
+- Warning/unmapped: `--warn: #ff9800`
+
+## Type and spacing
+
+- UI type: Segoe UI with Malgun Gothic fallback
+- Filename type: Consolas with D2Coding fallback
+- Control height: `--krea-control-height: 38px`
+- Content width: `--krea-content-width: 1200px`
+- Row gap: 12px desktop, stacked fields below 700px
+
+## Responsive layout
+
+- Above 980px: four columns (file, original strength, character, applied strength)
+- 701–980px: two columns
+- 700px and below: one column; header actions wrap; the global tab strip scrolls inside its own container
+
+## Interaction
+
+- Filenames and source strengths are read-only.
+- Character name and applied strength are editable.
+- Save is disabled until a value changes.
+- Focus rings use the existing accent with `--krea-focus`.
+- Reduced-motion preference disables button transitions.
+
+## Resolution control
+
+- Uses the existing primary surface, border, input, type, and spacing tokens.
+- Width and height are editable numeric fields above the LoRA rows.
+- Desktop and tablet use a two-column control grid; mobile uses one column.
+- Validation is explicit: 256–4096 pixels and multiples of 8.
+
+## Preset routing control
+
+- Uses the existing `--surface`, `--krea-row`, `--krea-input`, `--border`, and `--accent` tokens.
+- Preset number and routing mode share `--krea-control-height`.
+- Character matching, selected always-on LoRAs, and disabled are mutually exclusive modes.
+- Always-on selections use compact filename, checkbox, and numeric strength rows; no new color or radius tokens are introduced.
+- Missing preset configuration is shown as LoRA disabled rather than inheriting another preset.
+- Desktop keeps the route header on one line; 700px and below stacks controls and selection rows.
